        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Kerma culture</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Homeland</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-nubia">Upper Nubia</a>, in present-day northern and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-sudan">central Sudan</a>, centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerma">Kerma</a>; at its height from the First to the Fourth Cataract; key sites Kerma with its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-deffufa">Western Deffufa</a>, Doukki Gel and Sai Island</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">Pre-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerma">Kerma</a> c. 3500–2500 BCE; Early Kerma c. 2500–2000 BCE; Middle Kerma c. 2000–1750 BCE; Classic Kerma c. 1750–1500 BCE; conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> c. 1504 BCE, with rebellions until c. 1300 BCE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-deffufa">Western Deffufa</a>, a monumental <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mudbrick">mudbrick</a> temple; great royal tumuli with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/human-sacrifice">human sacrifices</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> skulls buried with kings; an army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archery">archers</a>; trade in gold, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebony">ebony</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/incense">incense</a>; the raid into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> c. 1575–1550 BCE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">How we know them</span><span class="info-stat-val">excavations at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerma">Kerma</a> by George Andrew Reisner (1920s) and Charles Bonnet; surveys along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> and before the Merowe Dam; Egyptian inscriptions and records; ceramic sequences; skeletal and dental studies; ancient DNA (2022)</span></div>
